# ADRs are TRACKED. The blanket `docs/adr/*` ignore was removed because it made
# the repository lie: `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` link ADRs as live
# architectural claims, and `scripts/checks/doc_paths.py` is a mandatory gate that
# treats every rooted path in those documents as a statement that the path
# EXISTS. A gitignored ADR is absent from every CI checkout, so the pointer is
# false in CI and the gate fails there — and only there, which is the worst place
# for a gate to fail. That defect was previously worked around by carving out
# ADR-0007 alone (via `!`); the root cause was the ignore itself, so the ignore
# went and seventeen untracked ADRs came with it. `tests/unit/scripts/test_adr_tracking.py`
# now fails if a referenced ADR goes untracked, so this cannot rot back.
# Local architecture review reports (working notes, not versioned)
*.html
.benchmarks
*.svg
.workbuddy-ai

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/
*.gate.lock*
AUDIT_*.md
# Perf ARTEFACTS only. The bare `perf_*` also matched SOURCE modules -
# src/benchmarks/perf_accounts.py was silently untracked, so the file the
# seeder and the load file both import was absent from the repo. Scoped to
# what it was written for: the generated CSVs and logs.
# Perf artefact DIRECTORIES. The old bare `perf_*` matched these by name,
# which is also why it silently matched src/benchmarks/perf_*.py. Restore the
# directory-level coverage explicitly and scope the file patterns below.
#
# SCOPED TO THE ROOT. Every pattern here is anchored with a leading slash so it
# matches a generated artefact at the repository root and nothing deeper. The
# unanchored forms were themselves a second bug: a bare `perf-*` added to fix the
# first one swallowed `perf-results/` wholesale, which silently untracked the
# measurement EVIDENCE - six RESULT-* directories, the 2,101.9 s RSS/CPU series,
# and the hand-written STATE.md. An ignore rule that hides the proof is worse
# than the untracked source module it was written to fix, so the directory is
# negated explicitly below rather than left to pattern subtlety.
/reports/perf_*/
/perf_*.csv
/perf_*.log
/perf_*.out
/perf_*.json
!src/benchmarks/perf_*.py
# Evidence is TRACKED. The RSS/CPU series is the answer to L-10 and the run
# artefacts are what every latency claim in STATE.md rests on; neither survives
# a clone unless committed. This negation is deliberately explicit rather than
# relying on the anchoring above to keep missing it - a leading `!` is the only
# way to be sure, and getting this backwards silently untracked the evidence.
!/perf-results/
tests/benchmarks/results
locust_baseline_NON_REPRESENTATIVE.md
